message: "If you use this archive, please cite it as below. Once a Zenodo DOI is minted it will be added here; until then cite the repository and the commit."
type: dataset
title: "The TEP Archive (August 2025 – September 2026): working records of the Terminal Equivalence Principle program, with Hecke eigenvalue tables, candidate Maass forms and numerical automorphy tests for the even icosahedral Artin representations of conductors 1951 and 2141"
authors:
  - family-names: Lenchus
    given-names: William C.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-12
repository-code: "https://github.com/wlenchus/TEP-archive"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
keywords:
  - Artin conjecture
  - even icosahedral Galois representations
  - Maass forms
  - Hecke eigenvalues
  - Heilbronn characters
  - Terminal Equivalence Principle
  - research archive
abstract: >-
  Curated public record of the TEP research program, August 2025 – September 2026, with per-file
  SHA-256 hashes and provenance. Includes exact Hecke eigenvalue tables for the even icosahedral
  Artin representations of conductors 1951 and 2141 (Doud–Moore), the candidate Maass forms of
  eigenvalue 1/4 built from them, pointwise automorphy tests on complete generating sets of
  Gamma_0(N), the Fricke constant identified with tau(chi)/(sqrt(N) a_N), adjoint L-functions and
  L(1, Ad rho), and a Heilbronn-type bound with an exact certificate; together with the framework's
  theorem notes, experimental dictionary, review ledger and errata. The Artin conjecture for these
  representations is not claimed. Documents CC BY 4.0; code MIT.
